  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy runs on untagged push; needs beta tag filters",
    "Explanation": [
      "pipeline_green is true: the workflow and all three jobs (build, test, deploy) are SUCCESS. behaviour_correct is false: this was an untagged API-triggered run on branch koans-09-tag-filters, yet deploy ran and succeeded. The requirement says untagged branch pushes must not deploy. fix_target_job is all_jobs and fix is filters_tags_only_beta. CircleCI does not run jobs for tag pushes unless that job has a tags filter, and that applies to every job in the requires chain. Deploy depends on test, which depends on build. So a tags filter on deploy alone would not make it run when beta-main-0.1.1 is pushed, because build and test would not run for the tag. Every job therefore needs a tag filter matching beta tags, e.g. tags: only: /^beta-.*/. Deploy also needs branches: ignore: /.*/ so that untagged branch pushes do not deploy. Allowing all tags would wrongly deploy alpha-* tags. Restricting to branches or relying on requires alone would not enable tag-triggered runs."
